### Sesión — login (OPEN: no lleva token)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3012/api

### Login con username -> 200 { access_token, token_type, expires_in, refresh_token, refresh_expires_in }
POST {{baseUrl}}/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "admin",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### Login con email (sin distinguir mayúsculas) -> 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "ADMIN@norte-creativo.example",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### Contraseña incorrecta -> 401 "Credenciales inválidas"
POST {{baseUrl}}/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "admin",
  "password": "mala"
}

### Usuario inexistente -> 401 con EL MISMO mensaje
POST {{baseUrl}}/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "no-existe",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### Faltan campos -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "admin"
}
